  "final_message": "Done. Built the shared event calendar on the provided Flask + Vite scaffold.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 SQLite under `./data` (tokens + hashed passwords survive restarts):\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201, 409 on duplicate), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 `{\"token\": ...}`); auth via `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, protected routes answer 401\n- `GET /api/events` \u2192 `{\"items\", \"total\"}`, sorted by start, optional `start_date`/`end_date` (bare dates span the whole day; events overlapping the range are included)\n- `POST` (201) / `GET /api/events/{id}` / `PUT` (full replace \u2014 omitted optional fields cleared) / `DELETE`; any signed-in user may edit any event, `created_by` is the creator\n- Naive date-times treated as UTC, offsets converted, all responses in `...Z` form; validation errors return 400 `{\"error\", \"message\"}`; also `/api/health` and SPA serving from `frontend/dist`\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, React + TS + Tailwind v4 utilities, `src/index.css` is the only CSS):\n- Register/sign-in modal (registers then auto-signs-in), header shows username + sign-out\n- Month/week/day views with \u2039 \u203a navigation, Today button, and period labels; clicking a day pre-fills the create form for signed-in users\n- Event click \u2192 detail sheet (times in UTC, location, description, creator); signed-in users get edit + delete-with-confirmation; create/edit forms use `datetime-local` pickers and display the API's validation messages\n\nVerified: 69 API assertions via Flask test client (all passing), gunicorn serving API + built assets on :8000, `npm ci` + `tsc --noEmit` + `npm run build` clean, and data persistence across a server restart.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
